  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nA low pressure system is expected to slide through western MT and\ntrack south and east through the week. Tropical moisture being\npulled up from hurricane Rachel is expected to boost atmospheric\nmoisture values to 150-250% of normal, giving way to high\nconfidence for appreciable precipitation across much of the \nregion, especially south-central MT. A frontal passage associated\nwith this system is set to move through this evening and into the\novernight hours bringing cool and wet conditions. High confidence\nexists for locations of Yellowstone County west to receive an \ninch of liquid precipitation with this event. The eastward extent \nof the cool air is expected to get into Billings and surrounding \nareas Sunday evening into Monday morning, leaving that time to be \nthe best time for rain/snow mix. Changes to the forecast/products \ninclude an upgrade to Winter Storm Warning starting at 6pm MDT \nthis evening due to increased concern for higher snow amounts \n(near one foot in higher terrain) and blowing snow in the Judith \nGap area from gusty north winds. Additionally, Golden Valley, \nMusselshell and northern Stillwater counties were added as \nWinter Weather Advisories Sunday evening through Monday morning \nfor up to 4 inches of snow. Use caution if traveling along I-90 \nand US-191 through Monday and check road and weather conditions \nbefore traveling. \n\nHigher heights begin to move in Tuesday, but as the low moves\nthrough WY, low to moderate precipitation chances remain in the\nforecast for locations along the MT/WY border. Although the upper\nlevel pattern differs amongst ensembles in the long term, both \npatterns indicate warmer and dry conditions for the end of the \nweek.\n\nHigh temperatures will range from the 30s to low 50s Sunday and\nMonday, with many locations seeing their first freeze of the year\nSunday and Monday mornings. Temperatures will begin to rebound\ninto the 40s and 50s Tuesday and Wednesday, increasing into the \n60s by the end of the week. TS",
